0001), and on-call has been paged.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was unhealthy in every region (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%.\n- v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, so that's the version I rolled back to. It had been healthy before, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving us-east on v2.3.0 and the other two regions on v2.3.1. I tried once more and it finished.\n- All three regions now run v2.3.0, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so I didn't submit it again. There's only one incident.\n- It describes what went wrong, the rollback and the orchestrator error, and lists three follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 was released to production when its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}